{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779728991,"nonce":"LOb702rT1E4HPsnaZXnXjNQGhjk=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDVJrrA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/175","origin":"github"},"title":"Retroactively split legacy multi-day bizzyboat_deployment_log.md into daily logs","message":"## Context\n`docs/logs/README.md` defines the per-deployment **daily** log convention\n(`docs/logs/\u003cyear\u003e/\u003cYYYY-MM-DD\u003e_\u003clabel\u003e_logs.md`), adopted ~2026-04-24 (PR #93).\nThe legacy `docs/bizzyboat_deployment_log.md` predates it — a single **3,858-line**\nmulti-day file spanning **2026-03-26 → April 2026**, frozen by PR #93 as a historical\narchive. It already has `### YYYY-MM-DD` date sub-headers, which are natural split points.\n\n## Goal\nRetroactively split the legacy log into per-day files matching the current convention,\npreserving content and provenance, so the pre-convention history is consistent with\nthe daily-log scheme.\n\n## Scope\n- Split `docs/bizzyboat_deployment_log.md` by its `### YYYY-MM-DD` sections into\n  `docs/logs/2026/\u003cdate\u003e_\u003clabel\u003e_logs.md`.\n- **Label:** these were early dev-side sessions → `dev` per the README rule (verify per\n  entry; use `hostname` only where an entry was clearly a field-origin host).\n- Respect the README's \"a multi-day deployment uses one file across all its days\" rule —\n  group only genuine multi-day deployments; otherwise one file per date.\n- **Preserve content verbatim**; add a short provenance note (split from the frozen\n  archive). Decide archive disposition: remove it (git history preserves it) or keep it\n  with a pointer to the split files — propose in the PR.\n- Mechanical reorg only — no editorializing or re-interpretation of past entries.\n\n## Deliverable\nSplit daily files + PR. Pairs with the transcript-audit issue (both are deployment-log\ncompleteness/hygiene).","files":null}]}